  m_text: Safa and Marwa are two small hills located within the Masjid al-Haram in
    Mecca. Pilgrims perform Sa'i, which is walking seven times between these hills,
    during both Hajj and Umrah. This ritual commemorates Hagar's search for water
    for her son Ishmael and represents perseverance and faith.
